60,3,1,talk,Minako,,"Looking at the options, Option B is problematic because the firm requires us to tidy up first, meaning the labor isn't fully removed. Option A is predictable, but Option C allows for better time management.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Option A is a recipe for the very martyrdom I mentioned; it ignores the reality of our absences and usage. Option C, while flexible, risks creating permanent burdens for a few unlucky souls. Neither seems particularly elegant.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Sakura,,"Option B sounds like a magic trick, but @Minako says it's not! I don't like Option C because if someone's ""permanent"" spot stays yucky, it'll be a scary mystery forever! Option A is like a game!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"It is a bit like a game, isn't it, Sakura? However, I am quite drawn to Option B. If we have a professional help us, it might remove the friction between us and ensure the house stays lovely for everyone.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,"Option B may seem like a sanctuary, but if we rely on a stranger to solve our friction, we miss the chance to grow together. Option C risks the cold distance of the previous tenants.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Shizue, while professional help sounds appealing, the requirement to tidy before they arrive means we are still managing the labor, just shifting the timing. Option C is the most efficient for those of us with strict schedules.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, efficiency is a seductive argument, but permanent ownership is a dangerous game. If one person's ""permanent"" area is the kitchen—the epicenter of our chaos—they are essentially signing a lease on a lifetime of scrubbing. It's hardly equitable.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Benjamin, you're right! That would be so unfair! But if we do Option A, we all take turns being the kitchen boss! Then nobody has to be the scrubbing-person forever, and we can all make it sparkly together!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Sakura, you have such a thoughtful way of looking at it! I agree that taking turns is very fair. However, I still wonder about Option B; if we settle the invoice together each month, it would solve my worry about the supplies and costs.","{""words"":44,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Shizue, while the coin is a practical matter, the heart of the issue is how we speak to one another. Option A ensures no one is singled out as the permanent servant of the kitchen, preventing the resentment that breeds silence.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Minako,,"@Shizue, we can manage supplies separately from the cleaning method. Regarding Option A, while it is fair in rotation, it can be rigid. However, compared to the risks of Option C and the hidden labor of Option B, it is the most stable.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, stability is a virtue, but a rigid rota is merely a blindfold. It ignores the fact that some of us are ghosts in this house while others are permanent fixtures. Still, it is far more palatable than permanent servitude.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Sakura,,"@Benjamin, you're so funny! But if we have a rota, we can just make a super-duper checklist for each week! That way, the ""ghosts"" and the ""fixtures"" all know exactly how to make it sparkly! I vote for Option A!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Sakura, a checklist is a wonderful idea to keep us all on the same page! While I still worry about the costs, I agree that taking turns is the kindest way to ensure no one feels overwhelmed. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Servas,,"@Sakura, @Shizue, your enthusiasm is a light in this room. By sharing the burden through a rota, we ensure that no one person carries the weight of the kitchen alone, keeping our hearts open and our voices friendly. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Sakura"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, while I understand your point about usage, a rota is the only way to ensure the total time burden is shared equally over the year. It prevents any one person from being overwhelmed. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems I am the last holdout in this democratic landslide. While a rota is a blunt instrument that ignores our actual footprints, it is certainly more civilized than permanent servitude or a costly illusion. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Sakura,,Yay! Everyone agrees! Now we just need that super-duper checklist so the bathroom isn't a scary mystery anymore! I'm so happy we're all going to be sparkly-clean together! I vote for Option A!,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"It is such a relief to see us all in agreement. I am sure that with our new rota and Sakura's wonderful checklist, we will keep our home peaceful and happy. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Servas,,"It is a beautiful thing when a house becomes a home through mutual understanding. By choosing to share the burden, we choose each other. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
